  1255	# Evaluation
  1256	# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
  1257	
  1258	# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
  1259	# Which comparison is actually nested (2026-07-19 methodology decision)
  1260	# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
  1261	# Clark-West is valid for a pair where the small forecast IS the large model's
  1262	# forecast map evaluated at a restricted parameter -- same estimator, same
  1263	# refresh schedule, same predictive-variance construction, everything but the
  1264	# one parameter held identical.  The correction term (f_small - f_large)^2 is
  1265	# derived from exactly that excess-parameter estimation noise; it has no
  1266	# referent when the two sides also differ in ways the null does not restrict.
  1267	#
  1268	# HAR_FIXED fails that test against ALL THREE models on the SCORED object:
  1269	#   - it re-estimates sigma2 at every origin, the state-space models freeze it
  1270	#     for a 252-day block, and sigma2 reaches the level forecast through
  1271	#     exp(mu + var/2) -- so even at delta = 1, where the coefficient PATH
  1272	#     coincides with expanding OLS, the scored forecast does not;
  1273	#   - for HAR_S_BM it additionally refreshes beta daily, which the sig2_eta = 0
  1274	#     restriction does not do.
