  2444	# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
  2445	# The gate that used to govern, and how it compares to the one that governs now
  2446	# (BLOCKER-1 of the 2026-07-19 round-2 review)
  2447	# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
  2448	# The round-1 fix moved TWO things at once: the BAR (1.645 -> 3.0) and the
  2449	# COMPARATOR (CW vs HAR_FIXED -> CW vs each model's own restriction).  README
  2450	# 8.2 then argued the new gate was strictly tighter "because t >= 3 is a subset
  2451	# of t > 1.645".  That argument is void: the two bars are applied to DIFFERENT
  2452	# statistics, so there is no set to be a subset of.  The claim has been
  2453	# withdrawn (see README 8.2) and replaced by these two mechanical objects.
  2454	LEGACY_GATE_T_CRITICAL = 1.645
